From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Chu <iamfredchu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:59:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] TOTK: frame step and render scale sites for 1.4.2

Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.2 (main 5cb42b1c...) packs from a derived profile,
so it had no frame step: the game kept its own present interval 2 while the
host presented at the profile's 60 fps, and the game ran at double speed
(LNPANDY/NX2Apple#303).

The frame step, the two readers of the integer fps, the D-pad menu fade and
the swapchain argument come from FPSLocker's config for this build
(5CB42B1CF25469FB.yaml). The two render scale sites were found by 1.4.3's
bytes: one match each, 0xc0 apart as on 1.4.3. By disassembly of 1.4.2's
main, all 9 sites hold the original instructions the stubs assert, and every
branch back lands on the next original instruction. The only difference is
the D-pad fade, which reads the menu entry through x25 and writes s9 on
1.4.2 (x24 and s10 on 1.4.3), so that stub now takes both registers from a
per-build site table. 1.4.3's output is unchanged: the same 140 events on a
recording context before and after.

game.tsv gets a `build v655360 1.4.2` row, the game note an "Update 1.4.2"
section, and docs/agents/game-patches.md is regenerated.

Measured on an M1 Max, macOS 27.0.1, with 1.4.2's main rewritten by this
change: DM_FPS_TARGET=60 holds 60.0 fps at 1.000 of real time from the
title on, DM_FPS_TARGET=30 holds 30.0 fps at 1.000; two gameplay runs past
the title (71 s and 115 s) held 1 vsync for every frame at 1.000 of real
time. test_patches, test_docs and test_nsp_incremental pass.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#793
Reason: Tears of the Kingdom 1.4.2 ran at double speed without frame step sites
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#303
